* --------------------------------------------------------------------
* SPICE models for Naef-Daenzer et al. 2005 miniature VHF transmitter
* --------------------------------------------------------------------

* ---- Crystal, Butterworth-Van Dyke equivalent circuit -------------
* Nominal 49.5 MHz crystal (tripled to 148.5 MHz nominal freq in the
* paper). Rm/Cm/Lm/C0 are TYPICAL values for a small overtone crystal
* in this range -- replace with your crystal's datasheet values
* (Rm, Cm, C0) if you have them; Lm is derived so f0=1/(2*pi*sqrt(Lm*Cm)).
*
* pin 4 --[Rm]--[Lm]--[Cm]-- pin 2
*   |________C0_________|
*
* pin 3 = Ground (GND)
* pin 1 = NC (Not connected / excluded from SPICE subcircuit)

.subckt XTAL_49M5 1 2 3
Rm 1 n1 30
Lm n1 n2 690u
Cm n2 2  0.015p
C0 1 2  3p
Rgnd 3 0 100Meg
.ends XTAL_49M5

.subckt XTAL150 4 2 3
Rm 4 a 40
Lm a b 56u
Cm b 2 0.02p
C0 1 2 3p
.ends XTAL150 

* ---- Monopole antenna, 13 cm, 148.5 MHz ----------------------------
* Electrically short monopole (h/lambda = 0.064) modeled as its
* feed-point impedance: radiation resistance in series with the
* antenna's self-capacitance, referenced to circuit ground (the
* animal/dummy body acts as the counterpoise, same as circuit GND).
*
*   Rr   = 40*pi^2*(h/lambda)^2           ~ 1.6 ohm  (radiation R)
*   Cant = 2*pi*eps0*h / (ln(h/a) - 1)    ~ 1.1-1.2 pF (self-C, 0.15mm wire)
*
* feed --[Rrad]--[Cant]-- 0 (circuit ground)
.subckt ANT_MONOPOLE_13CM feed
Rrad  feed  n1   1.6
Cant  n1    0    1.2p
.ends ANT_MONOPOLE_13CM

* ---- Optional: larger antenna variant, e.g. for a bigger animal ---
* Same construction, scaled for a longer wire; adjust h below as needed.
* h = 0.30 m -> h/lambda = 0.149 -> Rr ~ 8.7 ohm, Cant ~ 2.0 pF (rough)
.subckt ANT_MONOPOLE_30CM feed
Rrad  feed  n1   8.7
Cant  n1    0    2.0p
.ends ANT_MONOPOLE_30CM